    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A western frontier fief of the Zhou kings that took over the old Zhou heartland in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wei-river-shandong">Wei River</a> valley.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shang-yang">Shang Yang</a>'s reforms from 356 BCE built a state of registered farmers, ranks earned in war and appointed officials.</li><li>King Zheng conquered the six rival states between 230 and 221 BCE and became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>'s First Emperor.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/records-of-the-grand-historian">Shiji</a> records that 177 people followed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duke-mu-of-qin">Duke Mu of Qin</a> into death in 621 BCE; a poem in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/classic-of-poetry">Book of Songs</a>, 'Yellow Bird', laments three brothers among them.</p></aside>
    </section>

